intro={
'purpose-momentum':('A reason you can act on','You do not need to learn everything today. You need a reason to begin and a next step you can repeat. Start with a problem you care about. It might be getting your business organized, making music, understanding AI, or building a useful resource. Name the person who benefits from your work. That person might be you, a customer, or a learner.','Purpose gives your work direction. A routine gives it a place in your week. A small experiment gives you something to review. These three things work together. If the plan does not fit your real life, change the plan rather than calling yourself a failure.','Begin by writing why the work matters to you and to the person you want to help. Choose a routine that fits your day. For example, practice for ten minutes after breakfast, then write one thing you learned. Review it at the end of the week and adjust what did not fit. Your task is to choose an action and notice what happens when you try it.'),
'ai-foundations':('Understand the tool before the task','AI is a broad name for computer systems that perform tasks we connect with intelligence. Generative AI creates material such as text, images, or sound. It learns patterns from data. A useful answer can still contain a mistake. A confident tone is not proof that the answer is correct.','An app is the tool you use. A model is part of the system that produces the result. A prompt is your request. Begin with a small task: ask for a draft of a short meeting agenda. Give the topic, the people involved, and the result you want. Read the draft and change anything that does not fit.','Learning AI is partly learning how to ask and partly learning how to check. Keep your own goal in view. Do not put private records into a tool just because it can accept them. Check the source when an answer makes an important claim. Start with one tool and one useful task before comparing a long list of products.'),
'everyday-ai':('Make room for the things that matter','Daily life involves many small tasks. Messages, appointments, job searches, family plans, and bills can compete for your attention. Technology can help you organize them. It cannot decide what matters most to you. Start by choosing one task that is repeated and often causes confusion.','A life flow is a simple set of steps for handling a recurring need. For example: collect the week’s appointments, check the calendar, choose available time, and make a plan. AI can help draft the plan. You still check the dates, travel time, and commitments.','We will focus on time, learning, money organization, work, communication, and digital judgment. For health, legal, or financial decisions, use reliable sources and qualified support where needed. AI can help you prepare questions and organize information. It should not turn missing information into a confident decision.'),
'small-business':('Start with the problem, not the logo','A business offers something that people find useful enough to choose. Before choosing a name, app, or website style, ask who has the problem and what they do about it now. You need to understand the customer before spending heavily on the solution.','A business plan explains what you offer, whom it helps, how you reach customers, and how the numbers work. Revenue is money the business brings in. Profit is what remains after the relevant costs. Cash flow is the movement of money into and out of the business. These ideas are related, but they are not the same.','Your first goal is a small test. Talk to potential customers, describe a clear offer, and learn what is missing. AI can help organize notes and draft questions. It cannot replace real customer responses. Use official sources to check registration, permits, and tax requirements for your situation.'),
'business-funding':('Know what the money needs to do','Funding is money used to support a business. The best first question is not how much you can get. It is what the money needs to accomplish and how the business would handle its cost. Buying equipment, paying operating expenses, and covering a temporary gap are different needs.','A loan must be repaid under its terms. Equity means giving an investor an ownership interest. A grant has specific requirements and is not available to every new business. A credit line can provide access to funds within its agreed limits. You need to read the actual terms rather than assume every option works the same way.','This course will teach preparation and comparison. AI can help build a checklist, organize verified figures, and draft questions. It cannot promise an approval or safely invent financial information. Confirm current requirements with the actual provider. InAct’s role on this site is education and commercial funding referral, not lending or approval.'),
'business-workflows':('Give the work a clear path','A workflow is a sequence of steps that takes work from a request to a result. Think about a customer inquiry. Someone receives it, checks what is needed, prepares information, reviews it, and replies. If the steps are unclear, software can make the confusion move faster.','Start by drawing the current process. Name the input, the expected result, and the person responsible at each step. Then identify repeated work. AI might draft a summary, sort requests, or prepare a checklist. A fixed rule might be enough for a simpler task.','An agent is a system that can take steps and use tools within its allowed limits. Its ability to do something is not the same as permission to do it. Keep review points visible. Try incomplete and unusual cases before trusting a process with important actions.'),
'digital-marketing':('Help people understand why your work matters','Digital marketing uses online channels to help people find and understand an offer. Social media is one part of it. Search, email, websites, and customer follow-up also matter. Posting more often is not a complete strategy. You need a clear audience and a useful message.','An audience is the group you want to help. Positioning explains why your offer fits their need. A customer journey is the path from first noticing the offer to taking a useful next step. Start with the question a person is trying to answer at each point.','AI can help draft ideas, outline posts, and organize a content calendar. You review the facts, the voice, and the fit with the audience. Measure actions that matter to the business. A view, a click, an inquiry, and a sale tell you different things.'),
'web-design':('Make a page that helps someone do something','A website is a set of files a browser can display. HTML gives the page its structure. CSS controls its appearance. JavaScript adds behavior. A domain is the address people use. Hosting is where the site’s files are made available. Learn these jobs before choosing a stack of tools.','Start with the visitor. What do they need to understand? What should they be able to do? A clear heading, useful navigation, and a working button can matter more than an elaborate animation. Movement should support the experience and allow people to use reduced motion when needed.','AI can help write code, but you still need to review the result. Check it on a phone, use the keyboard, and test the links and forms. A form that looks complete might not send anything. A saved note might stay only in one browser. Honest behavior is part of good design.'),
'music-ai':('Learn the industry before adding the generator','The music industry connects creative work with listeners. Songs can be written, performed, recorded, released, promoted, and used in many ways. A songwriter, producer, performer, label, publisher, and distributor can do different jobs. One person or team may do more than one of them.','A song and a recording are different things. Think of a song as the words and musical composition. A recording captures a particular version. That distinction helps explain credits, permissions, and how people are paid. We will introduce the terms slowly before moving into the details.','Technology has changed the industry many times: printed music, recordings, radio, downloads, streaming, and now generative tools. AI adds new ways to make and shape material. It does not remove the need to listen, choose, explain the project, and check release requirements. Start with the industry map, then explore the deeper AI lessons when the basic roles make sense.'),
'learning-products':('Make something that helps a person learn or act','A useful digital product helps a person do something they could not do as easily before. It might be a lesson, checklist, journal, template, or small app. Start with the user’s problem and what they already know. The product’s job should be clear before you generate a large amount of content.','A learning outcome describes what the learner should be able to do. An example shows the skill. Practice lets them try. Feedback helps them improve. A quiz can support learning, but it should not be the only chance to apply the idea. Questions can appear throughout the experience.','AI can help draft explanations and activities. You check accuracy, reading level, accessibility, and the match with the learner’s need. Then test the product with a real person. A polished file is a beginning. A useful learning experience comes from what the person can understand and apply.')}
for c in courses:
 n=c['order'];slug=c['id'];h,p1,p2,p3=intro.get(slug,('Begin with a useful decision','This course introduces the basic ideas before asking you to apply them. Start with the published foundation lesson and use its worked example to make the unfamiliar terms concrete.','You can choose this course independently. The related courses offer other directions when you need them; they are not prerequisites.','The curriculum shows what we are building next. Planned topics are clearly labeled, so you can distinguish the introductory lesson from the larger course.'))
 modules=[]
